{
  "name": "whisker",
  "title": "Whisker - controller for the Petoi Nybble robot cat, compatible with the OpenCat firmware",
  "revision": "A",
  "brief": "Drop-in controller for Petoi's Nybble (wooden robot cat), compatible with the Petoi Nybble / OpenCat firmware unmodified (NyBoard_V1_2 build): ATmega328P-AU at 16 MHz and 5 V with the Uno bootloader; PCA9685 at I2C 0x40 driving the 11 Nybble servos on their firmware channels through 3-row right-angle headers on the back at the stock grid; MPU-6050 at 0x68; 64 Kbit EEPROM at 0x54; buzzer D5, IR receiver D4, LED D3, NeoPixel D10, four Grove sockets (I2C, A2/A3, D8/D9, D6/D7), battery sense on A7. Improvements: USB-C with a CH340C and DTR auto-reset (the 6-pin dongle socket stays), reverse-polarity and TVS protection on the whole 2S battery input, a 3 A synchronous buck to 5 V, USB that powers only the logic rail, 660 uF of low-ESR bulk plus 10 uF per group on the servo rail, a Raspberry Pi 2x5 at the stacking position. Outline: the stock 64.8 x 55.4 mm footprint with its top notch, 58.0 x 49.0 mm hole pattern.",
