    "notes": "Outline: the stock NyBoard V1 footprint (spec 2.2, photo-measured, +-0.5 mm on edges) pulled in 0.1 mm per side: 64.6 x 55.2 mm, top lobes at 55.3, notch x 6.4-44.8 with its floor at 49.6 (spec y). The notch's right edge sits 0.1 mm inside the photo's 44.9 so the Pi socket's pads keep 0.5 mm to the edge at the Pi's own pin positions. Copper keep-outs at the four holes cover the 7 mm boss (spec 2.7). 4 layers: F.Cu / In1 routing, then a 5V pour / In2 routing, then a VBAT pour / B.Cu, poured GND (it carries 36 mm of track). No plane while routing: the servo headers and the battery socket sit on the back, and Freerouting mirrors a back part's layer stack, so a through-hole pin whose In1 shape route.strip_plane_pin_shapes dropped reaches the router with an In1 shape again (2026-10-02, In1 as the GND plane: every pair of same-net pins on the back headers stayed unrouted, J11-3 to J11-4, J11-5 to J11-6, 26-30 open). With no plane all four layers route, and In1 is poured GND after a measured 0 open."
  },
